# Outreach Engine — Cursor Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16 App Router (not Pages Router — never suggest pages/)
- TypeScript strict mode throughout
- Prisma + PostgreSQL for data
- Vercel AI SDK (ai package) for all LLM calls — not raw fetch to Anthropic
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Zod for all input validation
- claude-sonnet-4-6 as the model string everywhere

## Code style
- Always use `async/await`, never `.then()` chains
- Prefer `const` over `let` everywhere possible
- Named exports for components, default exports only for Next.js pages/layouts
- No `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow, or define the type
- Zod schemas live in `/lib/schemas/` and are shared between client and server
- All database access goes through `/lib/db/` — never import prisma directly in a route or component

## File structure conventions
- Server actions go in `/app/actions/` with `'use server'` directive
- API routes go in `/app/api/[route]/route.ts`
- Reusable components in `/components/`
- Business logic (agent loop, scoring, prompts) in `/lib/ai/`
- Prisma client singleton in `/lib/db/client.ts`
- All prompts as exported constants in `/lib/ai/prompts.ts` — not inline strings

## AI / agent loop
- Use Vercel AI SDK `streamText` with tools for the research loop
- Model is always `claude-sonnet-4-6` via `@ai-sdk/anthropic` provider
- All prompts are in `/lib/ai/prompts.ts` as template functions that take typed params
- Never hardcode API keys — always `process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`
- Firecrawl calls go through `/lib/scraper.ts` — one wrapper, not scattered inline

## API routes
- Always validate request body with Zod before using it
- Return consistent error shape: `{ error: string, code: string }`
- Use HTTP status codes correctly (400 for validation, 401 for auth, 500 for unexpected)
- No business logic in route handlers — call into `/lib/` functions

## Database
- Never call `prisma.$queryRaw` unless there's no Prisma query equivalent
- Always select only needed fields — no `findMany` without `select` on large tables
- Migrations via `prisma migrate dev` — never edit the database directly

## Deployment target
- Hosting on Railway, not Vercel
- No Edge Runtime anywhere — always standard Node.js
- No next/headers or next/cookies edge-only APIs
- Environment variables come from Railway dashboard, not .env.local in production

## Version-specific notes
- Next.js 16.2.6+ — use proxy.ts not middleware.ts, Node 20.9+ required
- Prisma 7.4.1 — ESM only, no binaryTargets, generator path changed from v6
  check actual generator config against prisma.io/docs before accepting Cursor suggestions
- Cursor's training data predates both — verify any scaffolded config files against official docs

## What to avoid
- Don't suggest `useEffect` for data fetching — use Server Components or Server Actions
- Don't use `fetch` in client components for mutations — use Server Actions
- Don't add auth until explicitly asked — single user MVP
- Don't install extra UI libraries (no shadcn, no Radix, no MUI) — plain Tailwind only
- Don't suggest `pages/api/` routes — App Router API routes only
